--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/rpc_tests/eth_commands/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Ethereum RPC tests
+
+
+tested:
+
+- eth_accounts
+- eth_blobBaseFee
+- eth_blockNumber
+- eth_call
+- eth_chainId
+- eth_feeHistory
+- eth_fillTransaction
+- eth_gasPrice
+- eth_getBalance
+- eth_getBlockByNumber
+- eth_getCode
+- eth_getHeaderByHash
+- eth_getHeaderByNumber
+- eth_getLogs
+- eth_getLogs
+- eth_getStorageAt
+- eth_getTransactionByHash
+- eth_getTransactionCount
+- eth_getTransactionReceipt
+- eth_getUncleByBlockHashAndIndex
+- eth_getUncleByBlockNumberAndIndex
+- eth_newFilter
+- eth_pendingTransactions
+
+
+
+## Usage
+
+1. go to path quranium-core/tests/rpc_tests/eth_commands then install node modules by`$ npm install`
+2.  Start a local GO node at `http://localhost:8545` (Replace the local node to testnet staging node )
+3. The nodes need the following state to work: https://github.com/ethereum/tests/blob/develop/BlockchainTests/bcRPC_API_Test.json
+
+
+### Running the Eth_commands tests
+To run the eth tests start the node(s) at the port described in `lib/config.js` (See [Start a node with a certain state] and run):
+
+    $ make test.eth
+
+### Running the Beacon_commands tests
+To run the Beacon tests
+
+    $ make test.beacon
+
+### Running the Validator_commands tests
+To run the Beacon tests
+
+    $ make test.validator
+
+
+**NOTE** you need to restart and reload the blocktests in the nodes, so that all pending and mined transactions get cleared from the test chain.
+
+
